---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout
  title="Support — HelloNotes"
  description="Getting started with HelloNotes, frequently asked questions, and how to get in touch."
  heading="Support"
  subheading="We’re happy to help."
  footerBadge="💬 info@hellotham.com"
  navLinks={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy' },
  ]}
  footerLinks={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy' },
    { label: 'GitHub', href: 'https://github.com/hellotham/hellonotes' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="my-6 rounded-card border border-line bg-card px-[26px] py-[22px]">
    Email us at <a href="mailto:info@hellotham.com">info@hellotham.com</a> and we’ll get back to you.
    For bugs and feature requests you can also open an issue on
    <a href="https://github.com/hellotham/hellonotes/issues">GitHub</a>.
  </div>

  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Launch HelloNotes and click <strong>Select Vault Folder</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Choose any folder of Markdown files — or an empty folder to start fresh. A new note is created
      with <strong>New Note</strong> (or <strong>⌘N</strong>).
    </li>
    <li>
      Write in Markdown. Type <code>[[</code> to link a note, <code>#</code> to add a tag, and
      <code>$…$</code> for math.
    </li>
    <li>
      Open the <strong>Graph View</strong> to see how your notes connect, and <strong>Ask Vault</strong>
      to get on-device answers grounded in your notes.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-bold">Where are my notes stored?</h3>
  <p>
    As plain <code>.md</code> files in the folder you selected. HelloNotes never moves them
    elsewhere; you can open them in any other app.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-bold">Do I need an account or the internet?</h3>
  <p>No. HelloNotes works entirely offline and has no account. Nothing is uploaded anywhere.</p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-bold">Why don’t I see the “Intelligence” features?</h3>
  <p>
    Summarise, Suggest and “Ask your vault” require a Mac with <strong>Apple Intelligence</strong>
    enabled (Apple silicon, a recent macOS, and Apple Intelligence turned on in System Settings).
    Everything else works without it.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-bold">Can I sync between devices?</h3>
  <p>
    Put your vault folder in any file-syncing location (iCloud Drive, Dropbox, etc.), or use the
    built-in Git features with your own remote. Your files, your choice.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-[18px] font-bold">What are the system requirements?</h3>
  <p>macOS 15 or later.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:info@hellotham.com">info@hellotham.com</a>.</p>
</DocLayout>
